    "content": "==== 3319a88e4f097d8c0bd83aa2b3500e9029e425b5\n3319a88e Fix memory allocation failure not being propagated correctly (#789)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: N/A\n==== e1f62ebe2dd8cdb229a10b481362e934a367be85\ne1f62ebe Fix some more undefined behaviour\nAs https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/784 notified me of\nundefined behaviour going undetected by the fuzzers, I ran the test\nsuite with the full undefined behaviour sanitizer enabled.\n\nThere is one bit of undefined behaviour that I cannot fix,\nFLAC__metadata_get_picture allows a picture type of -1 to mean all,\nbut this isn't part of the enum.\n==== a628cca3054c9fa62c4bc3d7355585326e5bfd1c\na628cca3 Remove null pointer arithmetic as it is undefined behaviour\nFixes https://github.com/xiph/flac/issues/784\n\nCo-authored-by: braheezy <11700503+braheezy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n==== aa414e46a040db63a7429bf46e704da1b41eb927\naa414e46 Limit amount of samples to decode in fuzzer_tool_flac (#783)\n\n==== a8adc6c0443144fecf9ff90c954e62eee4ce369c\na8adc6c0 Check for overflow in off_t when parsing chunks (#781)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/42537590\n==== 0ef3a5d8fae0ae1cb80a0a5bbd4710f510fb0ced\n0ef3a5d8 Silence a few 'may be used uninitialized' warnings\n\n==== c786b1cd16665a4335563bae13070beed7f1c547\nc786b1cd Fix another endless loop in chained ogg handling (#772)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: N/A (local run)\n==== 7e0c04c4b007aef354718e6180dfd7e01df7fba7\n7e0c04c4 Fix endless loop when skipping link (#765)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: N/A (local run)\n==== e3a7157b7415c8c7221ac7f05da1c54a8047d183\ne3a7157b Fix heap overflow under out-of-memory conditions ... (#764)\n... and use realloc of linkdetails more efficiently. This should\nreduce the number of fuzzer timeouts for fuzzer_seek\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/379254072\n==== 7f46eb20ab53410e96654449749fcc057893b7bd\n7f46eb20 Fix -Wunused-result warning for ID3v1 detection\n\n==== fd09bbb857ef1e44cf91188bc244c36f9314f751\nfd09bbb8 Fix end-of-stream signal not being propagated\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/370597904\n\n==== 3725add64a6363281d6fe40f5f9ef3fbb6097e36\n3725add6 Convert unused seekpoints in template to placeholders (#754)\nSee https://lists.xiph.org/pipermail/flac-dev/2024-October/006671.html\nfor details\n==== 155e206f0235c142c35e42365de2c3027b34a6c8\n155e206f Speed up undefined behavior fuzzing of decoder (#753)\n\n==== 2a23a2af844224c3065d3a65825ea83611dc3a47\n2a23a2af Address signed integer overflow (#751)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/42526392\n==== ed4e1c464ee178d99ebe53048ac66e9ed833b1c6\ned4e1c46 Don't try to skip link after allocation failure (#752)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/371233030\n==== 00a270848c7499c2cc46d53bad7db7d27e8ff8a3\n00a27084 Free metadata if subsequent allocation fails (#750)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/42538223\n==== 86d6de66a406b66271811a7d2ce35bd684682dae\n86d6de66 Disable fuzzer_tool_flac for i386 (#749)\nRevert commits ce91056 and 33b9a4a, disable tool_flac fuzzer for\ni386 ASAN because weird bugs keep popping up\n==== 50efa0c8cdf94438e8d64e7ccd60adfd2bbdab18\n50efa0c8 Improve allocation of linkdetails, check more often (#748)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/370562609\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/371068253\n==== 40ca8c73f3d0bd14495f157a67148a3f9bc67a28\n40ca8c73 Only fail on memory allocation after initializing other variables (#747)\nAs this issue was not reproducible, this might not actually be a\nfix.\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/42538252\n==== a89875d8b1c1595f90af8b4b22085bd18d7f7e04\na89875d8 Fix memory leak in flac command line tool (#746)\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/42538282\n==== e4f1ee9fff3b169d428cf4a3ff344919602b0243\ne4f1ee9f Fix signed integer overflow in seeking code (#745)\nAlso add some more seeking tests\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://issues.oss-fuzz.com/issues/369652821\n==== b8efde21323a37f921e25d1dc8ce3d137a9c1539\nb8efde21 Add two error statuses to the stream decoder for broken files (#744)\n\n==== 4234fa772b3b3ae8ff02d05f911589149a6f095a\n4234fa77 Add FLAC__stream_decoder_skip_single_link and use in seeking\nThis commit adds the capability to find the end of a link through\nseeking instead of by reading forward, which should be much more\nefficient. It also exposes this capability through the new API\nfunction FLAC__stream_decoder_skip_single_link\n\nThis commit includes additions to the test suite and fuzzers\n\n==== d5a43acbfff454331ce7f7a33ce439f3ace55451\nd5a43acb Reduce chance of ogg serial number collision\nWhen two ogg streams were made with two different calls to `flac`\nwithin the same second, their serial numbers would be the same.\nThis caused problems with seeking in the test suite. While in\ntheory, libFLAC should be able to seek in a chained stream with\ntwo equal serial numbers without fail, in practice seeking in\nchained streams is hard enough. So, this commit makes sure the\nchained test files have links with unequal serial numbers.\n==== dd9c48b69c44acd345bf59880993c56611e4e1e0\ndd9c48b6 Use Ogg end of stream marker when decode-chained-stream not enabled\n\n==== 9dd1b0a6a184b33433e4edb3bb381e36c4366c63\n9dd1b0a6 use ogg_page_granulepos to get number of samples written for Ogg FLAC (#743)\nCo-authored-by: Martijn van Beurden <mvanb1@gmail.com>\n==== e42f723b124a8451fa5ae9c404529f2d876da8cf\ne42f723b Remove debug messages (#741)\nWhen compiled with NDEBUG defined, the test suite output was\nextremely noisy. As both these debug messages have served me no\nuse the last few years, it is time to remove them.\n==== e50c876a1c0348c23f26b2ee348a2dee40c9d23b\ne50c876a Do not try to apply replaygain when bps changes\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: N/A\n\n==== 33b9a4a765376aad75436b61c5509f0097368167\n33b9a4a7 Work around i386 ASAN null pointer bug\nFor some reason, i386 ASAN does not copy a pointer somewhere in the\ncode. Using gdb I get a mention of a synthetic pointer, so perhaps\nthe compiler instrumented with ASAN thinks this pointer isn't\nused. Anyway, commit adds a check for that null pointer which\nisn't necessary otherwise and is only activated for i386 ASAN.\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\n==== defad5b5442550a9bd678076fe7ad125edb9f087\ndefad5b5 Turn replaygain application off when impossible\nAddition to commit 808efb3. That commit threw a warning, but did\nnot actually turn off replaygain application.\n\nCredit: Oss-Fuzz\nIssue: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=70482",
